{"title":"Career Roadmap · Oncology Technician","role":"Oncology Technician","summary":"An Oncology Technician supports the delivery of cancer-care services, particularly in departments involving radiotherapy, radiation treatment equipment, patient preparation, treatment-room workflow, safety procedures, and treatment documentation.","facts":{"Current degree":"Allied Health Sciences (B.Sc / BPT / BOT / BMLT etc.)","Course":"Radiotherapy Technology"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"An Oncology Technician supports the delivery of cancer-care services, particularly in departments involving radiotherapy, radiation treatment equipment, patient preparation, treatment-room workflow, safety procedures, and treatment documentation."},{"type":"p","text":"Within a Radiotherapy Technology pathway, the role is closely associated with radiation oncology teams and may involve supporting:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"External beam radiotherapy"},{"text":"Simulation and treatment preparation"},{"text":"Patient positioning and immobilization"},{"text":"Radiation treatment equipment"},{"text":"Treatment-room procedures"},{"text":"Brachytherapy support"},{"text":"Imaging guidance"},{"text":"Quality and safety procedures"},{"text":"Patient communication"},{"text":"Treatment documentation"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The professional works as part of a multidisciplinary oncology team involving radiation oncologists, medical physicists, radiation therapists/technologists, nurses, dosimetrists and other healthcare professionals."},{"type":"note","label":"Qualification and scope note","text":"“Oncology Technician” is a broad job title. A generic B.Sc/BPT/BOT/BMLT qualification does not automatically qualify someone to independently operate radiotherapy equipment or perform radiation-therapy procedures. Students targeting this career should complete a recognized Radiotherapy/Radiation Therapy Technology education and supervised clinical training appropriate to the jurisdiction and employer. Radiation-related duties must always follow applicable licensing, accreditation, radiation-safety and institutional requirements."}]},{"heading":"Recommended Career Pathway","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"UG / Recognized Radiotherapy Technology Education"},{"type":"flow","items":["Anatomy","Physiology","Oncology Fundamentals"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Radiation Physics + Radiobiology"},{"type":"h","text":"Radiotherapy Equipment Training"},{"type":"h","text":"Clinical Internship"},{"type":"h","text":"Oncology / Radiation Therapy Technician"},{"type":"h","text":"Senior Radiation Therapy Technologist"},{"type":"h","text":"Specialized Radiotherapy Professional"},{"type":"h","text":"Senior / Supervisory / Technical Role"},{"type":"h","text":"Management / Research / Advanced Technology"}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Career Stage","Primary Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Medical and scientific foundation"}],[{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"Radiation science and oncology"}],[{"text":"Year 3"},{"text":"Equipment and clinical radiotherapy"}],[{"text":"Year 4"},{"text":"Clinical internship and specialization"}],[{"text":"Entry Level"},{"text":"Patient preparation and treatment support"}],[{"text":"Experienced"},{"text":"Complex treatment workflows and equipment"}],[{"text":"Senior"},{"text":"Quality, safety, supervision"}],[{"text":"Advanced"},{"text":"Specialized oncology technology, research or management"}]]}]},{"heading":"Year-by-Year Roadmap","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Medical Foundation"},{"type":"h","text":"Build strong knowledge of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Human anatomy"},{"text":"Human physiology"},{"text":"Medical terminology"},{"text":"Pathology"},{"text":"Basic pharmacology"},{"text":"Patient care"},{"text":"Infection prevention"},{"text":"Healthcare ethics"},{"text":"Communication skills"},{"text":"Basic emergency care"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Oncology Foundation"},{"type":"h","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"What cancer is"},{"text":"Benign vs malignant tumours"},{"text":"Tumour growth"},{"text":"Metastasis"},{"text":"Cancer staging"},{"text":"Common cancer types"},{"text":"Cancer risk factors"},{"text":"Basic cancer diagnosis"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Major cancer categories:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Breast"},{"text":"Lung"},{"text":"Head and neck"},{"text":"Prostate"},{"text":"Cervical"},{"text":"Colorectal"},{"text":"Brain and CNS"},{"text":"Lymphoma"},{"text":"Leukaemia"},{"text":"Skin"},{"text":"Paediatric cancers"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Radiation Science"},{"type":"h","text":"Develop a strong foundation in:"},{"type":"h","text":"Radiation Physics"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Atomic structure"},{"text":"Radioactivity"},{"text":"X-rays"},{"text":"Gamma rays"},{"text":"Electrons"},{"text":"Photon interactions"},{"text":"Radiation dose"},{"text":"Energy"},{"text":"Attenuation"},{"text":"Scattering"},{"text":"Radiation measurement"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Radiobiology"},{"type":"h","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Cellular response to radiation"},{"text":"DNA damage"},{"text":"Tissue response"},{"text":"Tumour response"},{"text":"Fractionation"},{"text":"Radiosensitivity"},{"text":"Repair"},{"text":"Repopulation"},{"text":"Reoxygenation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Radiation Protection"},{"type":"h","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Time"},{"text":"Distance"},{"text":"Shielding"},{"text":"Controlled areas"},{"text":"Personal monitoring"},{"text":"Radiation warning systems"},{"text":"Exposure prevention"},{"text":"Contamination principles"},{"text":"Emergency procedures"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — Radiotherapy Technology"},{"type":"h","text":"Develop practical understanding of:"},{"type":"h","text":"Treatment Equipment"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Linear accelerator"},{"text":"Cobalt teletherapy systems"},{"text":"CT simulator"},{"text":"Treatment couch"},{"text":"Immobilization systems"},{"text":"Brachytherapy equipment"},{"text":"Radiation detectors"},{"text":"Treatment imaging systems"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Modern Techniques"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"3D conformal radiotherapy"},{"text":"IMRT"},{"text":"VMAT"},{"text":"IGRT"},{"text":"SRS"},{"text":"SBRT"},{"text":"Image-guided positioning"},{"text":"Adaptive radiotherapy fundamentals"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Patient Positioning"},{"type":"h","text":"Learn the importance of:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Reproducibility"},{"text":"Immobilization"},{"text":"Treatment alignment"},{"text":"Reference marks"},{"text":"Patient comfort"},{"text":"Organ protection"},{"text":"Position verification"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 4 — Clinical Internship & Professional Readiness"},{"type":"p","text":"The final stage should focus heavily on supervised clinical experience."},{"type":"h","text":"Clinical Exposure"},{"type":"h","text":"Gain exposure to:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Radiation oncology department"},{"text":"CT simulation"},{"text":"Treatment planning workflow"},{"text":"Linear accelerator"},{"text":"Brachytherapy"},{"text":"Patient positioning"},{"text":"Treatment verification"},{"text":"Radiation safety"},{"text":"Treatment documentation"},{"text":"Quality assurance"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Final-Year Objective"},{"type":"p","text":"The student should understand the complete treatment pathway:"},{"type":"h","text":"Patient Referral"},{"type":"h","text":"Oncology Consultation"},{"type":"h","text":"Diagnosis / Staging"},{"type":"h","text":"Radiotherapy Decision"},{"type":"h","text":"Simulation"},{"type":"h","text":"Immobilization"},{"type":"h","text":"Imaging"},{"type":"h","text":"Treatment Planning"},{"type":"h","text":"Plan Verification"},{"type":"h","text":"Patient Setup"},{"type":"h","text":"Image Verification"},{"type":"h","text":"Radiation Treatment"},{"type":"h","text":"Monitoring"},{"type":"h","text":"Documentation"},{"type":"h","text":"Follow-Up"},{"type":"p","text":"Actual treatment prescription, planning approval, dose decisions and clinical interpretation remain the responsibility of appropriately qualified professionals."}]},{"heading":"Radiation Therapy Workflow","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A technician/technologist may support the operational workflow under authorized protocols:"},{"type":"h","text":"Treatment Schedule"},{"type":"h","text":"Patient Identification"},{"type":"h","text":"Treatment Verification"},{"type":"h","text":"Patient Preparation"},{"type":"h","text":"Immobilization"},{"type":"h","text":"Positioning"},{"type":"h","text":"Image / Setup Verification"},{"type":"h","text":"Treatment Delivery"},{"type":"h","text":"Patient Observation"},{"type":"h","text":"Treatment Documentation"},{"type":"h","text":"Next-Fraction Preparation"},{"type":"h","text":"Critical Safety Checks"},{"type":"p","text":"Before treatment, verify according to institutional protocol:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Correct patient"},{"text":"Correct treatment site"},{"text":"Correct treatment plan"},{"text":"Correct treatment fraction"},{"text":"Correct positioning"},{"text":"Correct immobilization"},{"text":"Required imaging verification"},{"text":"Equipment readiness"},{"text":"Safety interlocks"},{"text":"Treatment-room status"}]}]},{"heading":"CT Simulation","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"CT simulation is a major component of modern radiotherapy."},{"type":"h","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Patient preparation"},{"text":"Positioning"},{"text":"Immobilization"},{"text":"CT acquisition"},{"text":"Reference marks"},{"text":"Scan protocols"},{"text":"Image transfer"},{"text":"Image registration fundamentals"},{"text":"Treatment-planning data transfer"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Workflow:"},{"type":"h","text":"Patient Identification"},{"type":"h","text":"Positioning"},{"type":"h","text":"Immobilization"},{"type":"h","text":"CT Simulation"},{"type":"h","text":"Image Quality Check"},{"type":"h","text":"Reference Marking"},{"type":"h","text":"Image Transfer"},{"type":"h","text":"Treatment Planning"}]},{"heading":"Linear Accelerator Fundamentals","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Understand the basic components and functions of a LINAC:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Electron source"},{"text":"Accelerating waveguide"},{"text":"Target"},{"text":"Primary collimator"},{"text":"Flattening/filtering systems where applicable"},{"text":"Multileaf collimator"},{"text":"Gantry"},{"text":"Treatment couch"},{"text":"Imaging system"},{"text":"Control console"},{"text":"Safety interlocks"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The technician should understand the purpose of each component without exceeding their authorized operational responsibilities."}]},{"heading":"Modern Radiotherapy Technologies","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"3D-CRT"},{"type":"p","text":"Uses three-dimensional imaging to shape treatment fields around the target."},{"type":"h","text":"IMRT"},{"type":"p","text":"Intensity-modulated radiation therapy allows radiation intensity to vary across treatment fields."},{"type":"h","text":"VMAT"},{"type":"p","text":"Volumetric modulated arc therapy delivers treatment while the machine rotates around the patient."},{"type":"h","text":"IGRT"},{"type":"p","text":"Image-guided radiation therapy uses imaging to improve patient positioning and treatment accuracy."},{"type":"h","text":"SRS/SBRT"},{"type":"p","text":"Highly precise radiation techniques used for selected clinical indications."}]},{"heading":"Brachytherapy Fundamentals","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Brachytherapy involves placing radioactive sources close to or inside the treatment target."},{"type":"h","text":"Learn:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Basic brachytherapy principles"},{"text":"Applicators"},{"text":"Patient preparation"},{"text":"Sterile workflow"},{"text":"Radiation safety"},{"text":"Source handling principles"},{"text":"Treatment-room safety"},{"text":"Patient monitoring"},{"text":"Emergency procedures"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Common applications may include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Cervical cancer"},{"text":"Prostate cancer"},{"text":"Breast cancer"},{"text":"Selected skin cancers"},{"text":"Other site-specific indications"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Because radioactive sources are involved, strict institutional and regulatory protocols are essential."}]},{"heading":"Radiation Safety","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Radiation safety is one of the most important competencies."},{"type":"h","text":"Core Principle"},{"type":"h","text":"Minimize Exposure"},{"type":"h","text":"Reduce Time"},{"type":"h","text":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Increase Distance"},{"type":"h","text":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Use Appropriate Shielding"},{"type":"h","text":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Follow Approved Procedures"},{"type":"h","text":"Technician Responsibilities May Include"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Following controlled-area procedures"},{"text":"Wearing required dosimeters"},{"text":"Checking warning systems"},{"text":"Following access restrictions"},{"text":"Reporting equipment abnormalities"},{"text":"Following emergency procedures"},{"text":"Maintaining radiation-safety documentation"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Never bypass an interlock or safety system to continue treatment."}]},{"heading":"Patient Care Skills","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Cancer treatment can be physically and emotionally demanding."},{"type":"h","text":"Develop:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Compassionate communication"},{"text":"Anxiety management"},{"text":"Privacy and dignity"},{"text":"Clear treatment explanations"},{"text":"Basic symptom recognition"},{"text":"Safe patient transfers"},{"text":"Mobility assistance"},{"text":"Infection prevention"},{"text":"Treatment compliance support"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Potential Treatment Effects"},{"type":"p","text":"Recognize and appropriately escalate symptoms such as:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Fatigue"},{"text":"Skin reactions"},{"text":"Nausea"},{"text":"Pain"},{"text":"Swelling"},{"text":"Appetite changes"},{"text":"Mucositis"},{"text":"Difficulty swallowing"},{"text":"Treatment-site discomfort"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The technician should recognize and report concerning symptoms rather than independently diagnosing or treating them."}]},{"heading":"Oncology Emergency Awareness","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Understand how to recognize and escalate potentially serious situations such as:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Severe breathing difficulty"},{"text":"Loss of consciousness"},{"text":"Severe bleeding"},{"text":"Seizure"},{"text":"Severe allergic reaction"},{"text":"Acute neurological deterioration"},{"text":"Severe dehydration"},{"text":"Sudden chest pain"},{"text":"Severe treatment reaction"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Follow institutional emergency protocols and immediately involve the appropriate clinical team."}]},{"heading":"Quality Assurance","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Radiotherapy requires exceptionally strong quality and safety systems."},{"type":"h","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Equipment QA"},{"text":"Calibration concepts"},{"text":"Daily checks"},{"text":"Safety interlocks"},{"text":"Imaging verification"},{"text":"Treatment-record verification"},{"text":"Incident reporting"},{"text":"Near-miss reporting"},{"text":"Preventive maintenance"},{"text":"SOP compliance"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Quality Workflow"},{"type":"h","text":"Equipment Check"},{"type":"h","text":"Verification"},{"type":"h","text":"Treatment Readiness"},{"type":"h","text":"Patient Safety Check"},{"type":"h","text":"Treatment Delivery"},{"type":"h","text":"Documentation"},{"type":"h","text":"Incident / Variance Reporting"},{"type":"p","text":"Detailed dosimetric calibration and acceptance testing are generally performed by appropriately qualified medical physicists and other authorized personnel."}]},{"heading":"Clinical Documentation","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Maintain accurate records related to:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Patient identification"},{"text":"Treatment schedule"},{"text":"Treatment fractions"},{"text":"Setup information"},{"text":"Imaging verification"},{"text":"Equipment status"},{"text":"Treatment interruptions"},{"text":"Patient observations"},{"text":"Safety incidents"},{"text":"Maintenance issues"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Accuracy is critical because radiotherapy involves repeated treatment fractions."}]},{"heading":"Skill Matrix","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Skill","Beginner","Intermediate","Advanced"],"rows":[[{"text":"Anatomy"},{"text":"✓"}],[{"text":"Oncology"},{"text":"✓"}],[{"text":"Radiation physics"},{"text":"✓"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"Radiobiology"},{"text":"✓"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"Radiation safety"},{"text":"✓"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"Patient positioning"},{"text":"Basic"},{"text":"✓"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"CT simulation"},{"text":"Basic"},{"text":"✓"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"LINAC knowledge"},{"text":"Basic"},{"text":"✓"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"Brachytherapy"},{"text":"Basic"},{"text":"✓"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"IGRT"},{"text":"Basic"},{"text":"✓"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"Treatment documentation"},{"text":"✓"}],[{"text":"Patient communication"},{"text":"✓"}],[{"text":"QA concepts"},{"text":"Basic"},{"text":"✓"},{"text":"Advanced"}],[{"text":"Digital systems"},{"text":"Basic"},{"text":"✓"},{"text":"Advanced"}]]}]},{"heading":"Technology Skills","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Essential"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Electronic medical records"},{"text":"Treatment management systems"},{"text":"Hospital information systems"},{"text":"Basic Excel"},{"text":"Digital documentation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Radiotherapy Technology"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"CT simulation systems"},{"text":"LINAC interfaces"},{"text":"Treatment-management systems"},{"text":"Image-guidance systems"},{"text":"Record-and-verify systems"},{"text":"Brachytherapy systems"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Advanced"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Treatment-planning-system fundamentals"},{"text":"DICOM"},{"text":"Medical image processing"},{"text":"Digital image registration"},{"text":"Basic data analytics"},{"text":"AI-assisted imaging concepts"}]}]},{"heading":"Final-Year Project Ideas","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Project 1 — Patient Positioning Accuracy"},{"type":"p","text":"Study variations in positioning and their effect on treatment reproducibility."},{"type":"h","text":"Project 2 — Radiation Safety Awareness"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop and evaluate a radiation-safety education programme for healthcare workers."},{"type":"h","text":"Project 3 — Immobilization Device Comparison"},{"type":"p","text":"Compare different immobilization approaches based on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Reproducibility"},{"text":"Comfort"},{"text":"Setup time"},{"text":"Stability"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 4 — AI-Assisted Image Registration"},{"type":"p","text":"Explore how computer vision could assist radiotherapy image alignment."},{"type":"h","text":"Reference Image"},{"type":"h","text":"+"},{"type":"h","text":"Daily Image"},{"type":"h","text":"Image Registration"},{"type":"h","text":"Alignment Analysis"},{"type":"h","text":"Potential Setup Deviation"},{"type":"h","text":"Project 5 — Radiotherapy Workflow Optimization"},{"type":"h","text":"Analyze:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Patient waiting time"},{"text":"Setup time"},{"text":"Treatment-room utilization"},{"text":"Documentation delays"},{"text":"Workflow bottlenecks"}]}]},{"heading":"Internship Strategy","kind":"internships","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Prioritize clinical exposure in:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Cancer hospitals"},{"text":"Radiation oncology departments"},{"text":"Comprehensive cancer centres"},{"text":"Medical colleges with radiotherapy departments"},{"text":"Radiotherapy technology centres"},{"text":"Oncology research centres"},{"text":"Radiation therapy equipment environments"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Internship Checklist"},{"type":"h","text":"Try to gain supervised exposure to:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"CT simulation"},{"text":"Patient positioning"},{"text":"Immobilization"},{"text":"LINAC workflow"},{"text":"IGRT"},{"text":"Brachytherapy workflow"},{"text":"Radiation safety"},{"text":"Treatment documentation"},{"text":"QA procedures"},{"text":"Patient communication"}]}]},{"heading":"Entry-Level Career Options","kind":"careers","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Depending on qualification, registration and employer requirements:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Radiotherapy Technician"},{"text":"Radiation Therapy Technologist"},{"text":"Radiation Oncology Technician"},{"text":"Oncology Technician"},{"text":"Radiotherapy Technologist"},{"text":"Radiation Therapy Assistant"},{"text":"Oncology Department Technician"},{"text":"Radiotherapy Clinical Assistant"},{"text":"Radiation Oncology Research Assistant"},{"text":"Cancer Care Technology Assistant"}]},{"type":"p","text":"For regulated radiotherapy roles, the candidate should verify the exact eligibility and professional title used by the relevant institution."}]},{"heading":"Employer Skill Matrix","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Employer","Most Valuable Skills"],"rows":[[{"text":"Cancer Hospital"},{"text":"Radiotherapy + patient care"}],[{"text":"Radiation Oncology Centre"},{"text":"Treatment workflow + safety"}],[{"text":"Medical College Hospital"},{"text":"Clinical + academic skills"}],[{"text":"Comprehensive Cancer Centre"},{"text":"Multimodality oncology"}],[{"text":"Research Centre"},{"text":"Data + clinical research"}],[{"text":"Radiotherapy Technology Company"},{"text":"Equipment + applications"}],[{"text":"Oncology Equipment Service"},{"text":"Technical equipment knowledge"}],[{"text":"Healthcare Technology Company"},{"text":"Digital oncology systems"}]]}]},{"heading":"Certifications & Learning","kind":"certifications","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Tier 1 — Essential"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Basic Life Support"},{"text":"First Aid"},{"text":"Radiation safety training"},{"text":"Infection prevention"},{"text":"Patient safety"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Tier 2 — Strongly Recommended"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Radiation therapy technology"},{"text":"Medical imaging fundamentals"},{"text":"CT simulation"},{"text":"Radiobiology"},{"text":"Radiation protection"},{"text":"Oncology care"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Tier 3 — Advanced"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Treatment-planning fundamentals"},{"text":"Medical image processing"},{"text":"DICOM"},{"text":"Healthcare data analytics"},{"text":"Clinical research"},{"text":"AI in medical imaging"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Certifications should complement—not replace—the recognized education and supervised clinical training required for regulated radiotherapy practice."}]},{"heading":"PG Options","kind":"pg_india","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Depending on the student's qualifying degree and eligibility:"},{"type":"h","text":"Clinical / Technology"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"M.Sc Radiotherapy Technology"},{"text":"M.Sc Radiation Therapy"},{"text":"Medical Radiology/Radiation Technology"},{"text":"Advanced Oncology Technology"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Healthcare"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Master of Public Health"},{"text":"Hospital Administration"},{"text":"Healthcare Management"},{"text":"Clinical Research"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Technical"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Biomedical Engineering"},{"text":"Medical Imaging"},{"text":"Medical Physics-related pathways where eligibility permits"}]},{"type":"h","tex